-   entry .Event   what the containerd client logs as it changes the daemon
+   entry .Event   o que o cliente containerd registra em log ao alterar o daemon

=   entry .Event   what the containerd client logs as it changes the daemon
-     detail
+     detail

-         Every change `Containerd` makes to the daemon is logged at `info`: `ContainerCreated(id)`,
-         `ContainerDeleted(id)`, `ImageDeleted(name)`, `TaskCreated(container)`,
-         `TaskStarted(container, pid)`, `TaskKilled(container, signal)` and
-         `TaskDeleted(container)`. All but `ImageDeleted` are tagged `Log.Process`;
-         `ImageDeleted` is tagged `Log.Resource`. Reads (`containers`, `version`, `task`, …) log
-         nothing. A `Containerd.Event is Loggable` must be in scope for every client method;
-         `logging.silentLogging` discards them.
-     entry .communicable   renders each event as a message, such as _started the task for container `web` as PID `4321`_
+         Toda mudança que `Containerd` faz no daemon é registrada em log em `info`:
+         `ContainerCreated(id)`, `ContainerDeleted(id)`, `ImageDeleted(name)`,
+         `TaskCreated(container)`, `TaskStarted(container, pid)`, `TaskKilled(container, signal)` e
+         `TaskDeleted(container)`. Todos, exceto `ImageDeleted`, levam a tag `Log.Process`;
+         `ImageDeleted` leva a tag `Log.Resource`. Leituras (`containers`, `version`, `task`, …)
+         não registram nada. Um `Containerd.Event is Loggable` precisa estar no escopo para todo
+         método do cliente; `logging.silentLogging` os descarta.
+     entry .communicable   renderiza cada evento como mensagem, como _started the task for container `web` as PID `4321`_

